{
  "note": "The (record, chain) unit payloads (spec 014, amended 2026-08-02). Each vector is a bytes-level accept/reject case for conversationUpdatePayloadSchema (schema: conversation-update) or conversationPayloadSchema (schema: conversation). The payload of a pn/conversation-update or pn/conversation envelope IS the unit: the record, plus — when the record is delegated-signed — the leaf-first grant chain that authorizes it. The schemas enforce well-formedness only: whether a present chain actually authorizes the record (subject, leaf key binding, abilities, the record-time expiry window) is the verifier profile in spec 014, evaluated where key logs can be resolved. Grant signatures here are shape-valid Signature strings, not verifiable signatures, and `proof` digests are the real spec-003 digests of the links they name.",
  "digestIdentity": {
    "note": "The chain sits ALONGSIDE the record, never inside it, so record identity is a function of `record` alone: digest(payload.record) is the same id whether `chain` is absent or present. This is what makes a re-delivered or relayed unit name the same digest in a commit binding as the authoring delivery did.",
